{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia","id":1036416,"title":"NATO vs Russia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-22T20:21:10-08:00","id":1036416,"title":"NATO vs Russia","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=Iwy_20EAx90\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=Iwy_20EAx90\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=Iwy_20EAx90\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=Iwy_20EAx90 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Watch the video to here someone talking sense here. The Democracts need to cool it on the Russia file, putting troops on Russia's border is a really bad idea. <br /> <br /> I didn't miss the first cold war we don't need a repeat because the Democracts are pissed Putin exposed their dirty laundry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T22:02:36-08:00","id":1036439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia#post1036416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Democracts need to cool it on the Russia file, putting troops on Russia's border is a really bad idea.<br /> <br /> I didn't miss the first cold war we don't need a repeat because the Democracts are pissed Putin exposed their dirty laundry.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've been trying to halt Russia's attempts to expand to the west for years, as it looks as if they're attempting to regain states lost when the USSR fell apart, or earlier, and they started with the Ukraine and have been amassing troops and weapons on the borders of other Eastern Bloc countries who have asked for America's help.<br /> <br /> You may not want a cold war, but the people of Lithuania likely don't want to be under the Soviet bootheel again, and we assured them way back in 1998 we would help them defend their independence. Plus they joined NATO a while back and deserve the organization's aid.<br /> <br /> This video you share is incredibly lopsided. I'm not sure who the man is but in his haste to insult this Maddow, he seems to not be aware of existing partnerships with these countries, or that Russia is the aggressor in this situation. His example of Russia putting troops on Mexico's border would only count if America was, before that, putting troops on Mexico's border right after annexing Cuba.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-23-2017, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T22:37:16-08:00","id":1036448,"title":"","content":"Russia already launched an invasion of Ukraine and started hacking our systems to manipulate our political process (I don't give a fuck who the Russians were hacking, the fact that they were hacking our political parties is B.A.D.) We need to make a very strong show of force to send them a clear reminder them that they can't just fuck around with our country and our allies like that and not expect consequences.<br /> <br /> Obama seriously dropped the ball in both situations - in fact, I dare say his failure to help Ukraine out is probably his biggest failing as president. Sadly however, I expect Trump is far more likely to fellate Putin's dick than take him to task, so you have no need to worry about any kind of cold war between Russia and the US Omega. The last thing that will happen with Trump in charge of the US is any kind of aggressive maneuvers against Russia. If anything Trump is more likely to disband NATO and let Russia swallow up all of their old countries.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* I do find it immensely funny though to hear Republicans talking about how we need to play nice with Russia and we can't get too aggressive with them. What happened to all the neocons? I generally didn't like those guys in a lot of ways, but the one thing I did trust them on was that they weren't going to just bend over and kiss Russia's feet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-23-2017, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T00:38:16-08:00","id":1036479,"title":"","content":"Fuck Russia and the bear Putin rode in on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T01:44:19-08:00","id":1036496,"title":"","content":"1) Never directly trust a video where someone directly cuts out 3 minutes of a broadcast without any explanation or acknowledgement of doing so. Seriously, the clip this guy plays jumps three minutes (you can tell by the clock ticker on the show), which eliminates whatever bridge Maddow put between the two topics. Usually that's done for the sole purpose of readjusting the narrative. Without the original broadcast at hand to compare it to, my inner skeptic says that guy probably didn't like a segue between the two points that would have blunted his outrage and called his interpretation of Maddow's segments into question (though all the ranting does plenty of that).<br /> <br /> 2) That video doesn't, in the slightest, establish any sort of grounds to blame the Democrats as a whole as responsible for a potential escalation. Admission into NATO isn't a solo US decision in the first place, and both parties oversaw agreements to expand NATO into former Warsaw Pact nations. Both parties today (even members of Trumps cabinet) support Obama's decision to increase troop deployments to NATO allies bordering Russia. Also... it's now in Republican hands. With control over the Congress and the Presidency, there's very little the Democrats can do to control the decision to escalate military power in Eastern Europe, or reduce it. They couldn't even effectively filibuster the decision in the Senate.<br /> <br /> 3) In the comparisons of what happened in Ukraine to what's worrying former Soviet states also generally skips an important factor: we don't have a general defense pact with Ukraine. Unless nuclear weapons are threatened or used against Ukraine, the US has no legal obligation to aid Ukraine in a military conflict. We have a standing pact via NATO to join in protecting them from armed aggression. If what happened in Ukraine happened to, say, Estonia we <b>have to</b> intervene unless we exit NATO first. Russia knows this. any armed attack by Russia on any NATO member nation is effectively declaring war on all the NATO nations (which is the whole point of NATO). You can't compare it to the Cuban Missile crisis. You can't compare it to Russia sending troops to Mexico's northern border. <br /> <br /> 4) Simplifying this to the Dems being pissy about the hacks is inane on multiple levels. First, that hacks should piss off everyone. Nothing's going to be good if next election some liberal hacker group spams the media with RNC/etc. emails and then the Republicans start calling foul. It's in everybody's best interest if foreign nations aren't trying to fuck with other nation's election outcomes (the US should stop doing that too...). Second, we responded to the hacks with... sanctions and diplomatic expulsions. The NATO troop increase is in response to our allies being nervous about military expansions by Russia and a very pro-Russia sounding US President. Third, if a bit repetitive, this is not actually a partisan move. Plenty of Republicans don't like Trump's soft talk on NATO obligations, and want more shows of force that we're not going to do what Obama did in Syria and Ukraine when it comes to nations that are our overt military allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:33:15-08:00","id":1036651,"title":"","content":"One of reasons why a lot of Poles are actually happy that Trump won is because they hope that he will have better relationships with Russia. Because if US provokes conflict with Russia, we are people who will suffer from it, not the US. This might be shocking for you, but from Eastern European perspective, US and Russia aren't that much different; two big evil powers. It's just that one is far away and willing to use us as their pawns, and other is closer and thus more threatening, so we ally with the first one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-23-2017, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T10:29:17-08:00","id":1036699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036651#post1036651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of reasons why a lot of Poles are actually happy that Trump won is because they hope that he will have better relationships with Russia. Because if US provokes conflict with Russia, we are people who will suffer from it, not the US. This might be shocking for you, but from Eastern European perspective, US and Russia aren't that much different; two big evil powers. It's just that one is far away and willing to use us as their pawns, and other is closer and thus more threatening, so we ally with the first one.</div> </div> </div> </div> A wonderful insight and as a Canadian who shares a massive border with the US, one I can sympathize with. <br /> <br /> As for the rest of you guys, you forgot the key part where the West helped overthrow a democratically elected Ukrainian government which happened to be pro Russian, to put in a compliant set of minions, with neo nazi ties. <br /> <br /> And Russia is not planning to invade Lithuania, the actions of Putins have been reactions to American aggression. I hope President Trump will cool things down with Russia, if Americans keep stirring things up, it will be nations like Poland and, Lithuania that will be caught in the middle. <br /> <br /> You guys, also forgot to mention NATOs expansionist behavior that began before Putin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:58:25-08:00","id":1036754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036651#post1036651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of reasons why a lot of Poles are actually happy that Trump won is because they hope that he will have better relationships with Russia. Because if US provokes conflict with Russia, we are people who will suffer from it, not the US. This might be shocking for you, but from Eastern European perspective, US and Russia aren't that much different; two big evil powers. It's just that one is far away and willing to use us as their pawns, and other is closer and thus more threatening, so we ally with the first one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good post from a different point of view, thank you for the insight. One of the things when we have better relations with Russia is that we are less likely to start shooting at each other. Also just because we do have better relations with Russia does not mean we can't say no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T12:14:14-08:00","id":1036761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036651#post1036651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of reasons why a lot of Poles are actually happy that Trump won is because they hope that he will have better relationships with Russia. Because if US provokes conflict with Russia, we are people who will suffer from it, not the US. This might be shocking for you, but from Eastern European perspective, US and Russia aren't that much different; two big evil powers. It's just that one is far away and willing to use us as their pawns, and other is closer and thus more threatening, so we ally with the first one.</div> </div> </div> </div>And which one of them actually did invade Poland, imprison hundreds of thousands of citizens, and then annex the country? Given what's happening in Ukraine now, and Crimea before that, and Chechnya before that, any Pole who thinks that Putin's Russia can be a good neighbor is a fool.<br /> <br /> I don't want to think of NATO as the only thing standing in the way of USSR 2.0, but that's how it looks to me from here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036754#post1036754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very good post from a different point of view, thank you for the insight. One of the things when we have better relations with Russia is that we are less likely to start shooting at each other. Also just because we do have better relations with Russia does not mean we can't say no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see better relations between the US and Russia, but I also believe that one of three things must happen for that to come true.<br /> 1. Vladimir Putin and everyone who supports him is removed from power.<br /> 2. The United States abandons its standards in support of international human rights, allowing Russia to militarily dominate its neighbors.<br /> 3. The reigning Russian government has a sudden change of heart, stops trying to blame foreigners for their domestic problems, and works to fight the crime, corruption, and crony capitalism that stifles their economy.<br /> <br /> Sadly, I think the second option is most likely at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 01-23-2017, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:24:15-08:00","id":1036833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036651#post1036651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of reasons why a lot of Poles are actually happy that Trump won is because they hope that he will have better relationships with Russia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems pretty naive. There's a big difference between &quot;less adversarial&quot; and &quot;better&quot; relationships. I'm pretty sure most Palestians would call for &quot;better&quot; relationships between the US and Israel that don't involve the US backing Israel no matter what the Israeli government does, even though that would a more adversarial position towards the current Israeli government.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036699#post1036699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the rest of you guys, you forgot the key part where the West helped overthrow a democratically elected Ukrainian government which happened to be pro Russian, to put in a compliant set of minions, with neo nazi ties.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... a wonderfully oversimplified and conspiratorial explanation of what happened. Ukraine was a hugely divided nation between those that wanted better relationships with the rest of Europe and those that wanted to maintain stronger ties to Russia. The West didn't overthrow the government of Ukraine, the President fled protesters (we do remember that in a President isn't the government, right?), and this resulted in the government more strongly flipped to parties opposed to the ousted President. Sure, the West enabled in all this - for example the EU (also, you know, not America...) could have flatly rejected a deal with Ukraine before the deal was tanked by pro-Russian Ukrainian politicians - but there wasn't some direct interference with election.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Russia is not planning to invade Lithuania, the actions of Putins have been reactions to American aggression. </div> </div> </div>How exactly was the annexation of Crimea spurned by anything the US did? Why are you treating NATO, the UN, and the EU as apparent US puppets that have no agency of their own?<br /> <br /> What part of Russia's slaughtering of non-combatants in Syria was the fault of US aggression?<br /> <br /> Painting Putin as simply seeing to Russia's defense is... basically only what RT is selling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You guys, also forgot to mention NATOs expansionist behavior that began before Putin. </div> </div> </div>What does &quot;before Putin&quot; mean?<br /> <br /> Before Putin was involved in Soviet/Russian international affairs? Nope. Putin was operating in that sphere for the KGB well before the first NATO expansion into former Warsaw Pact nations discounting the negotiated unification of Germany and Germany's joining of NATO (since the USSR agreed to that one). Before Putin was involved in civilian politics? Also a nope. He moved from the KGB to being a civilian politician working in international affairs right before the NATO expansions. Before he was President? Sure but what exactly is important about that?.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036754#post1036754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things when we have better relations with Russia is that we are less likely to start shooting at each other. Also just because we do have better relations with Russia does not mean we can't say no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I think it's important to remember that &quot;better&quot; isn't the same as &quot;permissive.&quot;<br /> <br /> What has so many people worried is because Trump says, &quot;better,&quot; but only talks, &quot;permissive.&quot; We need to be ready to do more than say no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T15:16:46-08:00","id":1036862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036761#post1036761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And which one of them actually did invade Poland, imprison hundreds of thousands of citizens, and then annex the country? Given what's happening in Ukraine now, and Crimea before that, and Chechnya before that, any Pole who thinks that Putin's Russia can be a good neighbor is a fool.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you aware that USSR did that with full approval of western allies, including US? And that our government in exile was ignored even before war ended, with our borders being discussed and decided without our consent? Or that western allies ignored our pleas to help Warsaw Uprising, in order to not annoy Uncle Joe who patiently waited for the city and it's people to burn, so they could easily install their own government? All while Allies ignored us because Roosevelt decided that he likes Uncle Joe more? Allied forces literally watched our captial burn - burn to the ground - for two months? Couple this with US's reputation of constantly seeking conflict under pretense of &quot;policing the world&quot; and &quot;protecting human rights&quot; and other things that are commonly believed to just be excuses for war profiteering, and...you can see why we can't really see US as &quot;good guys&quot;, right? <br /> We are next to your traditional enemy, and you are offering us to allow you to put guns and rockets and bases in our territory for our protection. It's understandable that we agree. It's also understandable that Putin will try to secure as much land as possible, because US can wage war on them by proxy, using nearby countries as landbound versions of carrier airships. Which makes us a strategical target and a threat towards Russia. Which makes them interested in potentially punking us. Which makes us more reliant on outside help and making us even more indebted to that help. So we pray that there won't be a &quot;border incident&quot;, no US provocation or Russian aggression, because while US might lose some people and probably end up making dollars and grabbing some influence from such conflict, we are going to pay for it in real damage, as we will be the battlefield. <br /> <br /> Again, Putin is no saint. US is no saint either. Whatever happens, both of you are players trying to make as much profit as possible; US has better PR and can spin the story better, while Russia is pretty much perceived as Kingdom Of Evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T15:42:09-08:00","id":1036874,"title":"","content":"Poland willingly joined NATO (and in 1999, so this wasn't like some sort of blind situation where the US's current reputation as a world power after the collapse of the Soviet Union and the Warsaw Pact was unknown). Poland said, &quot;yes, please use your military power to help us protect our borders from enemy aggression.&quot; Russia was shouting mad about that before it happened citing how it was a threat to them, etc. etc. You personally might not have had any say in this, but Poland as a nation stopped being a bystander when they joined the modern incarnation of the Allies. Poland isn't a neutral nation, it picked a side, choosing to have military allies at the risk of military enemies.<br /> <br /> Also... increased deployment of active troops to NATO puts those troops under NATO control, not the US's control. If Poland is worried about deployments, they can ask NATO to do something else with them whenever they want and the US can only try to oppose it to NATO (which generally does not like to force member nations to agree to military deployments within their borders as an institution).<br /> <br /> Whatever the US's reputation is, and however justified that reputation is, Poland allied itself to the US through NATO. Poland doesn't get to play innocent now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T15:52:37-08:00","id":1036877,"title":"","content":"???<br /> I think you are misunderstanding. After we broke free from Soviet control, we pretty much had no choice other than align politically with something to ensure our security. And NATO was the best bet. That's hardly questionable. We just hope that US shoving their guns down Russia's throats won't result in a reflux that will directly hurt us. <br /> ...then again, our Minister of Security is a quite controversial person who would probably gladly lead the charge against Russians, but that guy is our own fault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:50:05-08:00","id":1036909,"title":"","content":"The Russians hacked both the DNC and the RNC and yet mysteriously did not release the RNC information. Can't imagine why. If you think that it's a political partisan issue well............there's an old Soviet Cold War term for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:51:22-08:00","id":1036912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036877#post1036877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">???<br /> I think you are misunderstanding. After we broke free from Soviet control, we pretty much had no choice other than align politically with something to ensure our security. And NATO was the best bet. That's hardly questionable. We just hope that US shoving their guns down Russia's throats won't result in a reflux that will directly hurt us.<br /> ...then again, our Minister of Security is a quite controversial person who would probably gladly lead the charge against Russians, but that guy is our own fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who lives in Japan, I know exactly what you mean. Those who supposedly have the benefit of &quot;distance&quot; don't seem to realize that the geopolitics of our reality make it very difficult for us to actually choose an alternative. As if we actually had an alternative. As with Poland, Japan certainly did not have much of a choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:09:46-08:00","id":1036923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036877#post1036877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">???<br /> I think you are misunderstanding. After we broke free from Soviet control, we pretty much had no choice other than align politically with something to ensure our security. And NATO was the best bet. That's hardly questionable. We just hope that US shoving their guns down Russia's throats won't result in a reflux that will directly hurt us.<br /> ...then again, our Minister of Security is a quite controversial person who would probably gladly lead the charge against Russians, but that guy is our own fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point when it comes to the situation in Eastern Europe, and give Russia some maneuvering room while it might not be the situation we want it just might be the best one. If we back Russia into a corner and they feel as if they have no options they will shoot and not ask questions. At that point any conflict will escalate quickly and we are all in trouble then. Now if we can have better relations with them or even &quot;permissive&quot; relations in areas which doesn't effect us, that might be the best option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:51:02-08:00","id":1036945,"title":"","content":"Remember that while I bitch about US, it's important to remember that NATO is definitively a good thing and there is definitively a need to keep certain forces in balance. Hand slapping Putin from time to time is good and important. It's just good to remember that it's easy to overdo it, and if US wanted to start a conflict with Russia, they could do it fairly easily by doing a well prepared provocation; with the public perception of Russia as Kingdom of Evil, you could swim an assault fleet into their waters, wait for them to take a first shot, spin it as a &quot;peaceful border patrol being attacked by vile Russians&quot;, and do whatever you consider profitable about it. <br /> And a lot of people here feared that Hilary Clinton would do exactly that. Would she? I don't know. Will Trump do? I don't know. I hope she wouldn't, and I hope he won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:05:03-08:00","id":1036954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036912#post1036912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who lives in Japan, I know exactly what you mean. Those who supposedly have the benefit of &quot;distance&quot; don't seem to realize that the geopolitics of our reality make it very difficult for us to actually choose an alternative. As if we actually had an alternative. As with Poland, Japan certainly did not have much of a choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do the Japanese worry about Chinese brinksmanship with the USA?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 01-23-2017, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:38:33-08:00","id":1036974,"title":"","content":"Ah, joys of innocent passage of warships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:57:58-08:00","id":1036987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036877#post1036877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are misunderstanding. After we broke free from Soviet control, we pretty much had no choice other than align politically with something to ensure our security. And NATO was the best bet. That's hardly questionable. We just hope that US shoving their guns down Russia's throats won't result in a reflux that will directly hurt us.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that the US isn't shoving our guns down Russia's throats. We increased our military commitments to NATO.<br /> <br /> You're saying that NATO is good... but the US giving NATO more troops and weapons... constitutes the US going out on its own to pick a fight with Russia.<br /> <br /> Can you see why I don't think your statements are fair here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036912#post1036912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who lives in Japan, I know exactly what you mean. Those who supposedly have the benefit of &quot;distance&quot; don't seem to realize that the geopolitics of our reality make it very difficult for us to actually choose an alternative. As if we actually had an alternative. As with Poland, Japan certainly did not have much of a choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Distance is also kind of a weird thing considering how close eastern Russia is to the USA and all.<br /> <br /> That said, Japan didn't have a choice in a much more direct sense given the terms of surrender from WWII.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:45:40-08:00","id":1037033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1036954#post1036954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Japanese worry about Chinese brinksmanship with the USA?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I am a chinese person living in japan. With that out of the way, let me say this:<br /> <br /> Like with most things, it really depends on who you talk to, the posturing happens of course. But the fact of the matter is that alot of business are looking to make inroads into China. The anime industry, for example, had a huge set back a few years ago due to territory spats that occured regarding senkaku islands. Fortunately that seems to be back on track and there are going to be some chinese-japanese productions and collaborations.<br /> <br /> However, most people actually are curious about china, there is actually no visible or really tacit hostility. Its just something that flares up, then dies down, and business' don't tend to like the flares. The filipinos, koreans, and chinese have somewhat of a presence in Japan, and for the most part they very happily work together, especially in traditional arts ( a recent chinese\\japanese play comes to mind that I watched).<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, I didn't really answer your question,oops. Umm, well, no, except for the usual political posturing such as with the south china sea, and the situation there. But thanks to the disruption by the new philiphines president and new connections in other ASEAN countries, the situation is calmer and very much in China's favor.<br /> <br /> So no, except within the geopolitical sphere. Business such as the the Japanese screen makers and other high end production want to continue the relationship with China and the U.S. ( for example the iphone and game consoles)<br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry, I have been ignoring the main topic.<br /> <br /> About that, interestingly Good U.S. and Russian relations may make it more feasible for the Kuril islands to be returned. Buts its difficult for us to make headway because we don't have a treaty and they see us as dependent on the U.S. ( and consideration my conversations with Japanese people, and how more subdued it is in the media compared to other disputed territories, they didn't expect anything, until perhaps now with such a shake up.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":1715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","user":"Ostarion","date":". 01-24-2017, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:31:16-08:00","id":1037314,"title":"","content":"I can't believe what I'm hearing, NATO is good?!?, I've been a lefty all my left no lefty I know of thinks NATO is good, what happened to the left? <br /> <br /> The USSR is history, NATO should be too, it's a relic of history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:40:38-08:00","id":1037322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037314#post1037314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe what I'm hearing, NATO is good?!?, I've been a lefty all my left no lefty I know of thinks NATO is good, what happened to the left?<br /> <br /> The USSR is history, NATO should be too, it's a relic of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you look at who is running the Russian Federation today, you'll find a lot of former Soviet officials forming a new oligarchy, following the same practices as their predecessors.<br /> <br /> Someday, maybe, when Russia develops a conscience and/or a commitment to peace, NATO can dissolve. For now, it still seems to be a necessary defense against a USSR that changed its name and wants to regain its old turf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T14:17:37-08:00","id":1037414,"title":"","content":"I constantly find it strange when people have this weird assumption that the &quot;left&quot; is some globally homogeneous group. Hell, the video that started this thread is basically, &quot;I consider myself a diehard lefty, and Rachael Maddow and I disagree with each other on something, therefore Rachel Maddow is a traitor to the left!&quot; Which silly (if highly profitable for those that want to appeal to the cleft in politics and use political tribalism for views, clicks, and money). The left is a coalition of a huge variety of groups, and varies highly from country to country as well. <br /> <br /> The idea that the &quot;left&quot; is anti-NATO seems like it could only come from a very narrow slice of what constitutes the left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T14:22:19-08:00","id":1037416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037314#post1037314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The USSR is history, NATO should be too, it's a relic of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>The USSR under that specific name might be history, but the Russian Federation acting like it did back in the old USSR days is still alive and well. Turn on the news, read newspapers, look for really any information about the actions of Russia under Putin and you'll see that plainly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T15:13:21-08:00","id":1037437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037322#post1037322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at who is running the Russian Federation today, you'll find a lot of former Soviet officials forming a new oligarchy, following the same practices as their predecessors.<br /> <br /> Someday, maybe, when Russia develops a conscience and/or a commitment to peace, NATO can dissolve. For now, it still seems to be a necessary defense against a USSR that changed its name and wants to regain its old turf.</div> </div> </div> </div> Russia could say the same for NATO, I'm no Putin fan, he's done horrible things, but let's not pretend it's all the Russians, and we have no responsibility at all for what's going on, we do, we've stirred shit up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T15:21:39-08:00","id":1037443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037314#post1037314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe what I'm hearing, NATO is good?!?, I've been a lefty all my left no lefty I know of thinks NATO is good, what happened to the left?<br /> <br /> The USSR is history, NATO should be too, it's a relic of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing wrong with having a military alliance between nations for the purposes of mutual protection, regardless of whether the USSR is still around or not. The NATO alliance has always been functioning and worked well, and it seems kind of silly to end it after 70 years just because the USSR isn't around anymore. There may be a few issues here and there that can be improved on, but it seems a little extreme to simply dissolve it.<br /> <br /> Remember that the first time Article 5 in NATO was ever invoked was after the 9/11 attacks on the US, and NATO carried its weight through Afghanistan.<br /> <br /> At the very least the US and member nations are each safer by being a part of NATO than they would be if they were left entirely to their own devices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T15:41:31-08:00","id":1037452,"title":"","content":"Depends on who you ask and their perspective.<br /> NATO is good because it provides you with backup of other countries and acts as a deterrent, promoting preace and tightening bonds of friendship.<br /> NATO is bad because we already tried formal alliances and guarantees before, and nobody cared, it leads into never ending budget draining vicious circle of arms against Russia which has to respond to it by matching it even if it doesn't really want to. That, and being tied to Earth's #1 warmonger, military industrial complex of US and their agenda of making money and securing resources through conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T15:46:53-08:00","id":1037454,"title":"","content":"First of all not bashing NATO here but one of the problems is most of the members are not pulling their weight. NATO asks that members spend 2% (I think) of their GDP on the military, but at present only 5 countries meet this requirement, and those are the US, UK, Estonia, Greece and Poland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T16:26:38-08:00","id":1037466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037452#post1037452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on who you ask and their perspective.<br /> NATO is good because it provides you with backup of other countries and acts as a deterrent, promoting preace and tightening bonds of friendship.<br /> NATO is bad because we already tried formal alliances and guarantees before, and nobody cared, it leads into never ending budget draining vicious circle of arms against Russia which has to respond to it by matching it even if it doesn't really want to. That, and being tied to Earth's #1 warmonger, military industrial complex of US and their agenda of making money and securing resources through conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div> Promoting peace? The wreckage that is much of the middle east says different. Call me old fashion, but I prefer diplomacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T16:36:34-08:00","id":1037472,"title":"","content":"As for making a big deal of Russia interfering with the American election their great act of interfernce wasn't creating a more informed public, important info they deserved to know. No ballot tempering, messing with parties bank account, no acts of terrorism, just simple truth telling.<br /> <br /> Compare that to the America recording to stirring up revolutions, over pushing the over throw of democratically elected governments in the Ukraine, in Grenada, attempts in Venesula, ect... <br /> <br /> What we need is for America to cool it's jets, stop acting so wounded, and push for better relations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T16:37:11-08:00","id":1037474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037466#post1037466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promoting peace? The wreckage that is much of the middle east says different. Call me old fashion, but I prefer diplomacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether NATO was around or not, the US still would have gone into Afghanistan, and certainly NATO had nothing to do with Iraq or the chaos in Syria or, indeed, much of anything in the Middle East outside of Afghanistan.<br /> <br /> You could certainly blame the US for all of that if you wanted, but I'm not entirely sure how you can point to NATO and say, &quot;This is your fault!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:40:15-08:00","id":1037511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037472#post1037472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for making a big deal of Russia interfering with the American election their great act of interfernce wasn't creating a more informed public, important info they deserved to know. No ballot tempering, messing with parties bank account, no acts of terrorism, just simple truth telling.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be news to you, but both sides were hacked. One side had their dirty laundry exposed. The other had a pro-Putin candidate that the Russians wanted to win. Yeah, it was kind of a big deal. I'm sure you'll still blame Trump winning on BLM and other &quot;alternative facts&quot; (love that phrase), but it was still primarily because of Russian interference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:02:41-08:00","id":1037523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037511#post1037511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be news to you, but both sides were hacked. One side had their dirty laundry exposed. The other had a pro-Putin candidate that the Russians wanted to win. Yeah, it was kind of a big deal. I'm sure you'll still blame Trump winning on BLM and other &quot;alternative facts&quot; (love that phrase), but it was still primarily because of Russian interference.</div> </div> </div> </div>The loss was squarely on Hillary's shoulders, due almost entirely to the baggage she brought with her - her emails (exacerbated by Bill Clinton's meeting with Loretta Lynch), her support for the TPP, her Wall Street speeches, her support for NAFTA, Benghazi, saying she was going to put coal miners out of business (even if that wasn't the full quote she should have realize how that would sound out of context) etc, etc. Those are what cost her the faith of the American public and with that, the election.<br /> <br /> The hacking of the DNC may have played a role, but at most t it was the proverbial &quot;straw that broke the camel's back&quot; - and it's important to remember that camel was already shouldering the load Clinton had piled on it well before the DNC hack happened. According to polls from June (a month before Wikileaks released the DNC files) almost 70% of Americans said she wasn't honest or trustworthy (in fact that same poll found that people felt Trump was slightly more honest and trustworthy!)<br /> <br /> Trying to handwave all of that by saying, &quot;She lost primarily because of the Russians,&quot; ignores all of the very real reasons why the American public did not like or trust her from the get-go, long, long before Russia's interference ever occurred. Hopefully the Democratic Party learns the lesson and never again tries to run a candidate who is so flawed in the eyes of the public (regardless of how unfair or &quot;real&quot; those flaws might be).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:04:41-08:00","id":1037526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037511#post1037511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be news to you, but both sides were hacked. One side had their dirty laundry exposed. The other had a pro-Putin candidate that the Russians wanted to win. Yeah, it was kind of a big deal. I'm sure you'll still blame Trump winning on BLM and other &amp;quot;alternative facts&amp;quot; (love that phrase), but it was still primarily because of Russian interference.</div> </div> </div> </div> I freely admit that the Russians had an agenda and worked towards self interest, but the Russians didn't make Hillary and the DNC act in the way they did, the Russians only exposed that they did so. <br /> <br /> And if Hillary hadn't tried to look tough by picking needless fights with the Russians, the Russians wouldn't have risked worsing relations with the Americans by interfering, the risk vs benifits would have added up very differently.<br /> <br /> So yes the Russians shaped the American election, but they did so my increasing transparency, not cheating.<br /> <br /> Was it one sided, yes, but they had good reason to do so, and it's nothing America wouldn't do, and in fact America has done worse, so the how dare they attitude just makes me roll my eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:24:08-08:00","id":1037540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037526#post1037526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I freely admit that the Russians had an agenda and worked towards self interest, but the Russians didn't make Hillary and the DNC act in the way they did, the Russians only exposed that they did so.<br /> <br /> And if Hillary hadn't tried to look tough by picking needless fights with the Russians, the Russians wouldn't have risked worsing relations with the Americans by interfering, the risk vs benifits would have added up very differently.<br /> <br /> So yes the Russians shaped the American election, but they did so my increasing transparency, not cheating.<br /> <br /> Was it one sided, yes, but they had good reason to do so, and it's nothing America wouldn't do, and in fact America has done worse, so the how dare they attitude just makes me roll my eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>'K. Addressing your points in order:<br /> <br /> * What did Hillary/the DNC do that was uniquely corrupt or intolerable, compared to other political campaigns? <i>Especially</i> compared to the Trump campaign?<br /> <br /> * Why do you think Hillary picked &quot;needless&quot; fights? What makes them needless?<br /> <br /> * The &quot;Increased Transparency&quot; was paired with a disinformation campaign that combined real content from the Clinton emails with some exaggerations and some outright lies. Are you aware of the Comet Ping Pong case?<br /> <br /> * It seems to me that the chief reason for Russian interference in the election was blatant self-interest on the part of the reigning government. Do you believe that Vladimir Putin's policies are good for Russia? Followup question - does America having been a douchebag before <i>in any way </i>justify the Russian Federation being a douchebag now?<br /> <br /> The most charitable interpretation of the Russian Federation's actions I could make is that they performed a multistage PR campaign in favor of the American candidate they wanted to win. Even if that wasn't &quot;cheating&quot;, it raises serious questions about conflicts of interest for that candidate and the integrity of our democracy itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 01-24-2017, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:32:26-08:00","id":1037544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037526#post1037526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it one sided, yes, but they had good reason to do so</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, to get the candidate they wanted elected. That was their only good reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037526#post1037526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and it's nothing America wouldn't do, and in fact America has done worse, so the how dare they attitude just makes me roll my eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>And when america has done that, the rest of the world gets pissed. As they should. And the nation whose political system we screwed with get pissed. As they should. Why would our own government not also get pissed when it happens to us? Add to that, the candidate the Russians backed is the one most likely to go to war with anyone and everyone just because he felt they did not respect him enough. He lashed out in the lead-up to the primaries, he lashed out in the lead-up to the election, and now that he's officially president? He's still lashing out. Yeah, I'd say it's a good reason to be pissed when the horse Russia backed is far more likely to start a world war because he feels slighted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:44:43-08:00","id":1037553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037540#post1037540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The most charitable interpretation of the Russian Federation's actions I could make is that they performed a multistage PR campaign in favor of the American candidate they wanted to win. Even if that wasn't &quot;cheating&quot;, it raises serious questions about conflicts of interest for that candidate and the integrity of our democracy itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember someone joking that Russia wanted to look like they back up Trump in order to sink him, and miscalculated. Gave me a good laugh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:52:09-08:00","id":1037602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037544#post1037544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, to get the candidate they wanted elected. That was their only good reason.<br /> <br /> <br /> And when america has done that, the rest of the world gets pissed. As they should. And the nation whose political system we screwed with get pissed. As they should. Why would our own government not also get pissed when it happens to us? Add to that, the candidate the Russians backed is the one most likely to go to war with anyone and everyone just because he felt they did not respect him enough. He lashed out in the lead-up to the primaries, he lashed out in the lead-up to the election, and now that he's officially president? He's still lashing out. Yeah, I'd say it's a good reason to be pissed when the horse Russia backed is far more likely to start a world war because he feels slighted.</div> </div> </div> </div> Of course Russia did that in favour of their self interest, as would America. <br /> <br /> Look America has thrown it's fit over it, now is the time having made your point to move on and stop pressuring Trump into making things worse, it's, time for everyone to cool off, and to rebuild diplomatic relations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:09:30-08:00","id":1037613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037602#post1037602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look America has thrown it's fit over it, now is the time having made your point to move on and stop pressuring Trump into making things worse, it's, time for everyone to cool off, and to rebuild diplomatic relations.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's time for America to double down and show Russia that they can't just muck around in our political process and expect to not even get a wrist slap out of it. Letting Russia do that and get away with it will merely encourages them to do it again next time. And frankly, I don't want Russian hacking and meddling with our political process to become the new normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:15:08-08:00","id":1037616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037602#post1037602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course Russia did that in favour of their self interest, as would America.<br /> <br /> Look America has thrown it's fit over it, now is the time having made your point to move on and stop pressuring Trump into making things worse, it's, time for everyone to cool off, and to rebuild diplomatic relations.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know that the big reveal of the extent of Russia's involvement wasn't even that long ago, right? I mean, it wasn't like it was a year ago or anything. And Trump didn't take office months back. This is all recent. I know it isn't what you want, but there it is.<br /> <br /> Also, just as an FYI? On behalf of US citizens everywhere, I promise that we, the public, never interfered in any foreign country's election. We, the public, never got involved in a regime change. We, the public, did not approve of those actions either. So when we, the public (some of us at least), are upset over it happening to us, it's because we, the public, never did those shenanigans, never were involved in those shenanigans, and are kind of mad to find out we, the public, had a candidate elected not by we, the public, but by an electoral college that we, the public, have no direct interaction with and by a foreign government that we, the public, have had no dealings with. I get you're now in favor of letting Trump do whatever he wants to do now and that you seem to love Russia and all it does for the world, but a majority of we, the public, do not.<br /> <br /> You have a habit of assuming entire groups of people are a single organism responsible for all the blame of a select few. It's a bad habit. To help you distinguish, I've over used we, the public.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:15:54-08:00","id":1037617,"title":"","content":"Given Trump selected - and the Republicans are set on confirming - Rex Tillerson for Secretary of State, the idea that our relationship with Russia is going to be good for anyone but certain people's pockets getting fuller is inane.<br /> <br /> As Trump himself has argued, you can't come to the negotiation table from a position of weakness... which is exactly what Trump is doing with Russia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:40:44-08:00","id":1037634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037616#post1037616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have a habit of assuming entire groups of people are a single organism responsible for all the blame of a select few. It's a bad habit. To help you distinguish, I've over used we, the public.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't you doing the same thing. Alot of what you are saying is misdirection. You are shedding the responsibilities of your country's actions by claiming that the political action was not backed up by the public. That there is a diversity among people, nations, and societies is true.<br /> <br /> So, where was this consideration when the phillipines were colonized.<br /> <br /> Where was this consideration when you dropped bombs in two cities in Japan.<br /> <br /> Where was this consideration when you overthrew the government of Iran in 1953.<br /> <br /> Where was this consideration when Europe was colonizing the rest of the world, and you sat by and watched, even doing a bit of colonizing of your own.<br /> <br /> I think what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said earlier is appropriate here. You don't get to play the innocent card now.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:47:49-08:00","id":1037637,"title":"","content":"Yeah. We, the US public, elected officials to undertake wars, regime changes and mess around with other nation's governments. And what's more, despite knowing this was going on, we the people proceeded to reelect those officials. Whether we're looking at Iraq, or Cuba or Lybia or wherever, the US has mucked around with a bunch of other nation's. And it's kind of unfair to go, &quot;Well since our elected leaders did those things and not the public, then the public doesn't have any responsibility for it, even though we elected and re-elected the people who did.&quot;<br /> <br /> The people of North Korea have no responsibility for what their government does, because they have no power over their government. The people of the US though? Yeah, we're responsible for the decisions our government makes, because we're the ones who put them in power to make those decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T21:59:11-08:00","id":1037663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037634#post1037634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said earlier is appropriate here. You don't get to play the innocent card now.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I largely agree, I think you're throwing a bit of a wide net to that point; enough to detract from it. There's plenty of shitty stuff the US has done during the post-WWII/Cold War era to point to. Things like, &quot;where was America during European Colonialism&quot; is not exactly a great point considering the answer is largely, &quot;still being a tiny post-colonial nation still trying to establish itself and it's own territory, and only had any real international power at the tail end of the primary periods of European colonial activity.&quot; Hold a country responsible for things from 100+ years ago without a bit more than throwing out that they happened gets a bit difficult to justify. The colonization of the Philippines started 200 years before the USA existed as a country, and the US didn't get directly involved with it until 100 years after that...<br /> <br /> I mean there's a plethora of examples from just the past 30 years where there's no questions that stem from the changes over the long course of history to make these points with. Esp. since &quot;democratically elected&quot; has changed drastically in what that means over that time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T22:01:49-08:00","id":1037665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037637#post1037637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. We, the US public, elected officials to undertake wars, regime changes and mess around with other nation's governments. And what's more, despite knowing this was going on, we the people proceeded to reelect those officials. Whether we're looking at Iraq, or Cuba or Lybia or wherever, the US has mucked around with a bunch of other nation's. And it's kind of unfair to go, &amp;quot;Well since our elected leaders did those things and not the public, then the public doesn't have any responsibility for it, even though we elected and re-elected the people who did.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The people of North Korea have no responsibility for what their government does, because they have no power over their government. The people of the US though? Yeah, we're responsible for the decisions our government makes, because we're the ones who put them in power to make those decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T05:44:18-08:00","id":1037782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037634#post1037634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't you doing the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple answer: No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037634#post1037634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alot of what you are saying is misdirection. You are shedding the responsibilities of your country's actions by claiming that the political action was not backed up by the public.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, no. I'm saying that when discussing the actions of a nation where leaders are elected, not every person elected that leader. Saying for instance &quot;Russia is evil because Putin&quot; is a falsehood. Putin is evil. The Russian people are not Putin, nor is Putin all the people. When discussing the actions of a nation, sure you can say &quot;the Russian government&quot; or &quot;Russia&quot; or what have you. But when discussing the citizens and what they have the right to complain about, generalizing an entire country by the actions of a single leader is misguided.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037634#post1037634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where was this consideration when you dropped bombs in two cities in Japan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna focus on this part here to make my point. Do you feel that the Japanese people have a right to be upset about Hiroshima and Nagisake? If you say no, they have no right to complain because of the attack on Pearl Harbor made by their government at the time, then you are correct in saying my statements were misdirection. If you say yes, the actions of their government does not prevent the citizens from having a right to disagree with their government and can still feel wronged, then you agree with me because those people are not the same entity who decided to attack Pearl Harbor and still have the right to disagree with their government.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T06:31:49-08:00","id":1037797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.truth-out.org/opinion/item/39159-noam-chomsky-on-the-long-history-of-us-meddling-in-foreign-elections\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://truthout.org/images/images_2017_01/2017_0119russia.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.truth-out.org/opinion/item/39159-noam-chomsky-on-the-long-history-of-us-meddling-in-foreign-elections\" target=\"_blank\"> Noam Chomsky on the Long History of US Meddling in Foreign Elections </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.truth-out.org/opinion/item/39159-noam-chomsky-on-the-long-history-of-us-meddling-in-foreign-elections\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.truth-out.org/opinion/item/39159-noam-chomsky-on-the-long-history-of-us-meddling-in-foreign-elections </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> US efforts to tip foreign elections have gone far beyond hacking &mdash; including financial support and assassinations. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Noam Chomsky on the long history of the US, interfering in foreign elections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T06:55:16-08:00","id":1037810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037782#post1037782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple answer: No.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, no. I'm saying that when discussing the actions of a nation where leaders are elected, not every person elected that leader. Saying for instance &amp;quot;Russia is evil because Putin&amp;quot; is a falsehood. Putin is evil. The Russian people are not Putin, nor is Putin all the people. When discussing the actions of a nation, sure you can say &amp;quot;the Russian government&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Russia&amp;quot; or what have you. But when discussing the citizens and what they have the right to complain about, generalizing an entire country by the actions of a single leader is misguided.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm gonna focus on this part here to make my point. Do you feel that the Japanese people have a right to be upset about Hiroshima and Nagisake? If you say no, they have no right to complain because of the attack on Pearl Harbor made by their government at the time, then you are correct in saying my statements were misdirection. If you say yes, the actions of their government does not preventthat citizens from having a right to disagree with their government and can still feel wronged, then you agree with me because those people are not the same entity who decided to attack Pearl Harbor and still have the right to disagree with their government.</div> </div> </div> </div> I never said that every American was personally responsible for it's governments actions, only that America as in the people, but not individuals, can't play innocent victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T07:21:38-08:00","id":1037826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037810#post1037810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said that every American was personally responsible for it's governments actions, only that America as in the people, but not individuals, can't play innocent victim.</div> </div> </div> </div>What <i>should</i> we do, pray tell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T08:06:01-08:00","id":1037844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037826#post1037826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <i>should</i> we do, pray tell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop pressuring Trump and just let Russia do all the things we shouldn't. I believe there's a 'stop whining about the election' thing in there too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-25-2017, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T11:45:04-08:00","id":1037942,"title":"","content":"You don't have to give Russia Carte Blanche, you just have to go to the table and talk things out instead of chest thumping. America has been the prime aggressor here, not Russia. <br /> <br /> I'm tired of this bullshit which is why I support Canada leaving NATO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:04:50-08:00","id":1037957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037942#post1037942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to give Russia Carte Blanche, you just have to go to the table and talk things out instead of chest thumping. America has been the prime aggressor here, not Russia.<br /> <br /> I'm tired of this bullshit which is why I support Canada leaving NATO.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you assess that the USA is the &quot;prime aggressor?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:23:33-08:00","id":1037976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037957#post1037957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you assess that the USA is the &quot;prime aggressor?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's absolutely true. Forget Russia's actions over the past decade. The only thing that matters is what Russia has done since they got the Savior of the Masses, the Hero of the Republic, Our Divine Leader Donald &quot;the Mighty&quot; Trump elected. Have they done anything to us since that glorious day? No! But what have we done? We, the dirty ignorant masses have had the audacity, the gall, to dare question Russia's action and to say cruel things about the Enlightened Ones, led by the Friend of All Men, the Rock Upon Which Greatness is Built, Vladimir &quot;Machismo&quot; Putin.<br /> <br /> How dare we prime aggressors in the United States, speak unkind words about such great men and their vision of a world of peace, prosperity, and equality for all straight rich white men?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:54:13-08:00","id":1037994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037957#post1037957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you assess that the USA is the &amp;quot;prime aggressor?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> The US pushed for the overthrow of a Democratic government in the Ukraine and things have spiralled out since then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T13:07:53-08:00","id":1037999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037994#post1037994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The US pushed for the overthrow of a Democratic government in the Ukraine and things have spiralled out since then.</div> </div> </div> </div>They supported an already existing attempt to overthrow the Democratic government that had shown its true colors as being aligned to Russia, who was ordering Ukraine's government to shut down protests and supplying them with weapons, which led to killings of protesters.<br /> <br /> The situation had already spiraled out of control when the United States stepped in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T13:34:00-08:00","id":1038017,"title":"","content":"Also, the US has had successful - if rocky and antagonistic - diplomatic relations with Russia for decades. We haven't stopped being at the table and talking with them. Boring diplomatic conferences rarely get media attention though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T14:17:19-08:00","id":1038037,"title":"","content":"Also, and this is not new info. Various state actions across the country as well as actions by the U.S. Congress increasingly show that what counts as the &quot;we the public&quot; when it comes to claims of culpability are an ever shrinking, less democratically chosen portion. (which has some truths, just rarely in the arena that some mention it) The U.S. is a less democratic place than some would want to believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T14:55:14-08:00","id":1038052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037942#post1037942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to give Russia Carte Blanche, you just have to go to the table and talk things out instead of chest thumping. America has been the prime aggressor here, not Russia.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're saying we just have to talk? All we have to do is talk to them? Just go to the metaphorical table and have a civil conversation and hash things out all peaceable-like? Wow. What a truly original solution to such an obviously silly problem. I'm honestly flabbergasted that literally no one has ever attempted that. Not once. Not ever. Its just crazy. Sure glad we had you here to cut this darned Gordian Knot. You should be in politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:28:40-08:00","id":1038124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037994#post1037994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The US pushed for the overthrow of a Democratic government in the Ukraine and things have spiralled out since then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this one of those 'alternative facts' I have have been hearing so much about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:00:07-08:00","id":1038134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1038124#post1038124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this one of those 'alternative facts' I have have been hearing so much about?</div> </div> </div> </div>It did happen.<br /> <br /> The President of the Ukraine was pushing for closer relations with Russia. Some people (mainly in western Ukraine and various oligarchs) were unhappy so they held a revolution. The US and most of western Europe sided with the revolutionaries (no surprise) since we wanted a pro-US government in Ukraine rather than a pro-Russian one. Unfortunately once all was said and done, the people of eastern Ukraine (who live in the Donbass region and who have always wanted closer ties to Russia) were understandably upset at the overthrow of the president they had elected. So they seceded from the rest of Ukraine to join Russia, and Russia decided to assist them.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's more at play than simple politics - Donbass has some pretty massive oil deposits which (thanks to advances in fracking) can now be accessed far easier and cheaper than a few decades ago. Western oil companies had been &quot;cut out of the loop&quot; by Ukraine's government (who was offering better contracts to Russian oil companies). So those western oil companies had been lobbying US and other European governments to reject Ukraine's president and accept the new revolutionary government. Unfortunately for them, by the time all was said an done, the Donbass region and it's oil deposits are now under de facto Russian control.<br /> <br /> There are lots of ways that this came together. As an example, then-Vice President Joe Biden's son, Hunter was working closely with Burisma Holdings (Ukraine's big oil company) which was unhappy with the Russian ties (since they felt that they could get better deals by working with western companies than the Russian government). Burisma Holdings initially came out on the side of the revolutionaries, though once it became clear that Donbass was going to be controlled by the Russians they started changing their tune. Still, Hunter Biden's dad, Joe, was one of the biggest pro-revolution voices in Washington D.C., gave lots of speeches about and applied a lot of pressure about how the US had to side with the Ukrainian revolutionary government, and it seems rather unlikely that his son didn't have some kind of influence on him.<br /> <br /> There were, of course, tons of other factors in play, but in general I would say that Omega is correct in that the US (and other European nations and various oligarchs) pushed for the overthrow of Ukraine's elected government, because the government was seeking closer ties with Russia and the situation certainly has spiraled out of control since then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:50:09-08:00","id":1038168,"title":"","content":"Installing governments friendly to your case while overthrowing unfriendly ones is nothing new and was pretty much turned into art by both sides due to how Cold War worked/is working.<br /> EDIT<br /> <a href=\"http://original.antiwar.com/justin/2016/12/11/stop-cia-coup/\" target=\"_blank\">http://original.antiwar.com/justin/2...stop-cia-coup/</a> not supporting it, not denying it, just throwing it as a food for thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-25-2017, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T16:37:04-08:00","id":1038640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1037782#post1037782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple answer: No.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, no. I'm saying that when discussing the actions of a nation where leaders are elected, not every person elected that leader. Saying for instance &quot;Russia is evil because Putin&quot; is a falsehood. Putin is evil. The Russian people are not Putin, nor is Putin all the people. When discussing the actions of a nation, sure you can say &quot;the Russian government&quot; or &quot;Russia&quot; or what have you. But when discussing the citizens and what they have the right to complain about, generalizing an entire country by the actions of a single leader is misguided.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm gonna focus on this part here to make my point. Do you feel that the Japanese people have a right to be upset about Hiroshima and Nagisake? If you say no, they have no right to complain because of the attack on Pearl Harbor made by their government at the time, then you are correct in saying my statements were misdirection. If you say yes, the actions of their government does not prevent the citizens from having a right to disagree with their government and can still feel wronged, then you agree with me because those people are not the same entity who decided to attack Pearl Harbor and still have the right to disagree with their government.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good, then let us stop equating nation-states to people.<br /> <br /> As to your question, I'll take the Japanese approach, which have no words for 'yes' and 'no', hence I disagree with the question. I suspect ( though I cannot be sure) that most Japanese people, who are the best qualified to address that question, would disagree with the question itself, or perhaps they might say a word that equates to the meaning of 'yes' and 'no' at once.( there are a few ways to do this).<br /> <br /> My point being that the question is self-defeating and is recognized as such in the context of the Japanese language.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T16:47:16-08:00","id":1038644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1036416-nato-vs-russia?p=1038640#post1038640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good, then let us stop equating nation-states to people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude... That was my entire damn point. That was what my entire damn post was driving home. The post you disagreed with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}